  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wildlife Without Borders-Amphibians In Decline</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of the Enigmatic and Highly threatened Lao Newt, Laotriton Iaeoensis, Phase II in Northern Laos. This is the second year of support to the Wildlife Conservation Society. This project will support a conservation effort for the Lao newt, by increasing the protection of the species from human overexploitation. Specific activities include: (1) conducting site visits to the areas that have been identified to have the optimum location with the best habitat, forest cover, stream, etc. to identify optimum areas to establish a community conservation area for the Lao newt; (2) increase public awareness by conducting an outreach campaign while working closely with the Xiengkuang local authorities. This campaign will focus on conservation education and aims to raise awareness about the species among villagers in the community, government officers, tourist agencies, and neighboring villages (3) petition CITES to list the Lao newt under Appendix III.</narrative>
  </description>
